course: dictionary
lesson: 7249
title: Patchy animals: piebald
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Piebald is a describing word. It tells you about an animal that has big patches of two colours, usually black and white. «She keeps a canary, several piebald mice and a restless revolving squirrel.» The word piebald tells you the mice are not all one colour.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The bracket says «patchy black and white», so piebald must mean patchy black and white. Check it by putting your meaning into the sentence: «She keeps a canary, several patchy black and white mice and a restless revolving squirrel.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Piebald can also be a noun, a name for the animal itself: «a piebald» is a horse or pony with black and white patches. Gypsy and Traveller horses are often piebald or skewbald, so you may meet these words in stories about horses and ponies.
fact: Piebald means having large patches of two colours, usually black and white.
fact: Piebald can be an adjective, as in «several piebald mice», or a noun, as in «a piebald» for a horse or pony.
fact: Skewbald is a similar word, but it means brown and white patches.
fact: Gypsy and Traveller horses are often piebald or skewbald.
exercise: «She keeps several piebald mice.» What does piebald mean? | Fluffy all over | Very fast | *Having big patches of black and white | Covered in glitter
exercise: Which animal is a piebald? | A squirrel in a revolving cage | A canary | *A horse or pony with black and white patches | A cloth on a chair
exercise: Mia says, «The piebald pony trotted into the field.» What colours might the pony be? | Plain grey with no marks | Pink and purple stripes | *Black and white patches | Bright green and yellow
test: «The piebald horse stood under the oak tree.» What does piebald tell you about the horse? | It is sleeping | It has no colour at all | *It has large patches of two colours | It is very tall
test: Ben says a piebald is a kind of cloth for a chair. Is he right? | Yes, a piebald is a cloth for a chair | *No, a piebald is an animal with patches, and the cloth is called an antimacassar | Yes, piebald means a cover | No, piebald means a bird
exam: The text says, «She keeps several piebald mice.» Which clue helps you most to work out what piebald means? | The word she | The word keeps | *The bracket saying patchy black and white | The word several
